CODEGEN.md §2.11, §3.5, DECISIONS 435: a Decode<N> part is a member of detail::AAccess, whose loader LoadPotions hides the record LoadPotions that a decoder body names (a local of Potion's extra list, a Decode0 parameter), so the record collides with the loader whatever Potion's width and whether or not its Decode is cut (g++: "'LoadPotions' is not a type").
-- a/a.canon --
package a

/// Named like the loader of the value potions; no value holds it, only a field of Potion does.
record LoadPotions {
  /// Its size.
  x: Int
}

/// A potion.
record Potion {
  /// Its key.
  name: String
  /// Its extras.
  extra: [LoadPotions]
}

/// The potions.
let potions: [Potion] keyed by name = [{ name: "a", extra: [] }]

emit cpp { out: "@features/a", namespace: "a", mode: data }
emit json { out: "out/" }
-- a.potions.json --
[{ "name": "a", "extra": [] }]
-- findings.txt --
error[E8005]  a/a.canon:18:5
  cpp: LoadPotions is generated for both a.LoadPotions and a.potions; rename one of them with @cpp(name:)

